    { "id": "l05.g.partitif", "type": "grammar", "title": "Du, de la, des", "titleEn": "\"Some\": the partitive article",
      "body": "For food and drink you take **some of**, French uses **du** (masculine), **de la** (feminine), **de l'** (before a vowel) and **des** (plural).\n\nAfter a **quantity**, it is always just **de** (or **d'**): un kilo de tomates, une douzaine d'œufs, beaucoup de pain.\n\nThe same after **avoir besoin**: j'ai besoin de pain.",
      "table": { "headers": ["", "Some…", "A quantity of…"], "rows": [
        ["masculine", "du pain", "une tranche de pain"],
        ["feminine", "de la confiture", "un pot de confiture"],
        ["before a vowel", "de l'eau", "une bouteille d'eau"],
        ["plural", "des œufs", "une douzaine d'œufs"]
      ] } },
    { "id": "l05.v.pain", "type": "vocab", "group": "Les aliments", "fr": "pain", "en": "bread", "pos": "noun", "gender": "m", "article": "du", "emoji": "🍞" },
